      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "This article describes the use of focus groups in research, including the advantages and disadvantages of using this type of research methodology. Using an example of a focus group of patients who experienced chronic pain, the authors discuss the planning, organisation, conduct and analysis of focus groups."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Focus groups enabled an exploration of the topics in-depth including obtaining insight from a patient's perspective of the management of their chronic pain. It was important and of value to take into account the experiences and expectations of health service delivery from a consumer's perspective."
        }
      ]},
